{
 "_source": "ours and LDT: loopws/logs/blog_handoff/figures_data.json, fig4_test_time_compute_maze (12:36, 10 Nov). HRM and TRM: worked out here with Davis et al. Appendix N's method, which gives exactly the paper's 13.7 GFLOPs per ACT step for HRM on Sudoku (t = 82, 24 layer applications).",
 "_how": "FLOPs per ACT step = t x layer applications x (8d^2 projections + 4td scores and values + 2*3*d*1536 SwiGLU), d = 512. HRM: t = 901 (900 cells + 1 puzzle-embedding position), 24 layer applications (H 2 x L 2 x 4 L-layers + 2 x 4 H-layers). TRM, attention, maze recipe (L_layers 2, H_cycles 3, L_cycles 4; baselines/trm_cfg_maze.yaml): t = 916 (16 puzzle-embedding positions), 3 x (4 + 1) x 2 = 30 layer applications (the paper's 42 for Sudoku is L_cycles 6). Both run their full 16 ACT steps at evaluation (Appendix N). Accuracies: Table 3 (Davis et al.'s retrains, best checkpoint chosen on the test set). Replace with the released-checkpoint sweeps when they land.",
